    "result": "Excellent! All tests are now passing. Here's a summary of the fixes:\n\n## Fixed Issues\n\n1. **Governance test (`src/finetune/governance.test.js`)**: \n   - **Problem**: Test imported `APPROVAL_STATUSES` as a named export from `./index.js`, but it wasn't exported.\n   - **Fix**: Added named exports for `APPROVAL_STATUSES`, `DATA_SENSITIVITY_LEVELS`, `GOVERNANCE_SECTIONS`, and `RISK_LEVELS` in `finetune/index.js` while keeping them in the default export for backward compatibility.\n\n2. **Evaluation test (`src/eval/index.test.js`)**:\n   - **Problem**: `toxicityMetric` function signature was `toxicityMetric(outputs, bannedTerms)`, but `runEvaluations` calls all metrics with `(outputs, references)`. This caused the references array to be treated as banned terms, incorrectly flagging safe outputs.\n   - **Fix**: Updated `toxicityMetric` signature to `toxicityMetric(outputs, references, bannedTerms = defaultBannedTerms)` so it accepts the references parameter but ignores it, using the default banned terms list instead.\n\n**Test Results**: \u2705 All 28 tests passing across 8 test files",
